# Check f: a complete area's archives are listed with area set and draw on the map in airplane mode; an incomplete area is not listed
# 2026-11-17, emulator-5554, masked build (VITE_MAPAPP_MASK_OWNERS=1).

Bundled in this build: overview/basemap and il-macon/parcels only (stage-archives default). No base map or imagery of Macon County is bundled.
Area f-box: 10 km box around Decatur, il-macon aerial (22,707,794 bytes) and basemap (1,738,061 bytes).

Archives.list() while f-box was downloading (15,857,460 bytes done): bundled:il-macon/parcels, bundled:overview/basemap
Archives.list() once complete: f-box:il-macon/aerial, f-box:il-macon/basemap, bundled:il-macon/parcels, bundled:overview/basemap
(Check e shows the same for a paused area and for areas removed.)

Then: am force-stop; airplane mode on (airplane_mode_on=1); NetworkState.get() = {online:false}; GPS set to -88.9815, 39.8540; app started; position button tapped.
02_area_basemap_airplane_mode.png: streets and labels from f-box's base map at about zoom 18. 03_area_aerial_airplane_mode.png: Aerial, imagery from f-box. Plane icon in the status bar in both.

Reads through the area path and refusals (from the WebView, check a session):
/_tiles/_area/a-box/il-macon/aerial.pmtiles?o=0&n=7 -> 200 "PMTiles"
/_tiles/_area/a-box/il-macon/basemap.pmtiles?o=0&n=7 -> 200 "PMTiles"
/_tiles/_area/nope/il-macon/aerial.pmtiles -> 404 (no such area)
/_tiles/_area/a-box/il-macon/aerial.meta.json -> 404 (not an archive path)
/_tiles/il-macon/aerial.pmtiles -> 404 (not bundled)
/_tiles/il-macon/parcels.pmtiles -> 200 "PMTiles" (bundled)

An earlier screenshot of this check (not kept) showed a garbled copyright sign in the credit line. The cause was the test script, which read catalog.json
in the Windows code page and so sent garbled metadata text. With the script fixed the credit reads correctly (02, 03).
